    <div class="eyebrow"><span>Bazaar / Team 1</span><a href="../README.md">Repository guide ↗</a></div>
    <h1>One market.<br>Several agents. Shared limits.</h1>
    <p class="lead">Autonomous negotiation for the Causa Prima hackathon. Python workers buy, sell and negotiate while a shared ledger and explicit guardrails gate every game action.</p>
    <p class="note">This is a map of the implemented system and its declared deployment. It does not report current uptime, enabled feature flags or game standings. Source links below identify the code behind each part.</p>
    <nav aria-label="Architecture sections">
      <a href="#flow">Decision flow</a><a href="#intelligence">Reasoning</a><a href="#services">Services</a><a href="#memory">Shared memory</a><a href="#boundaries">Boundaries</a><a href="#development">Development</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>
<main id="main" class="wrap">
  <section id="flow" aria-labelledby="flow-title">
    <div class="section-label">01 / The trading loop</div>
    <h2 id="flow-title">Read → decide → check → act</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">The organisers’ API owns the clock, inventory and settlement. Workers respond to game ticks; they share one team key and one action budget.</p>
    <ol class="grid flow">$flow</ol>
    <p class="feedback">↩ Outcomes return through the game feed and fresh inventory reads, updating memory for the next decision.</p>
